founder|[sound:3-3a.mp3]\n{gsar gtod mdzad mkhan/} Founder, initiator (H)\nSyllables: {sar/} = new, as in: {tshig gsar/} = vocabulary, new words, {lo gsar/} = Tibetan New Year; {gtod pa/} = to aim, to focus; {mdzad pa/} = to do (H) as in: {mdzad sgo/} = ceremony; {mkhan/} = nominaliser, showing the “doer” of an action\n-----\nExample: [sound:3-3b.mp3]\n {thon mi sam b+ho Ta yi sngon la bod la yig skad tog tsam byung yod na yang /_bod pa tshos khong yig skad gsar gtod mdzad mkhan rtsis kyi yod red/}  Although Tibet had a (lit. some) written language before {thon mi sam b+ho Ta/}, Tibetans regard him as the founder of their writing system.
initiator|[sound:3-3a.mp3]\n{gsar gtod mdzad mkhan/} Founder, initiator (H)\nSyllables: {sar/} = new, as in: {tshig gsar/} = vocabulary, new words, {lo gsar/} = Tibetan New Year; {gtod pa/} = to aim, to focus; {mdzad pa/} = to do (H) as in: {mdzad sgo/} = ceremony; {mkhan/} = nominaliser, showing the “doer” of an action\n-----\nExample: [sound:3-3b.mp3]\n {thon mi sam b+ho Ta yi sngon la bod la yig skad tog tsam byung yod na yang /_bod pa tshos khong yig skad gsar gtod mdzad mkhan rtsis kyi yod red/}  Although Tibet had a (lit. some) written language before {thon mi sam b+ho Ta/}, Tibetans regard him as the founder of their writing system.
father’s name|[sound:3-4a.mp3]\n{yab kyi mtshan/} Father’s name (HH)\nSyllables: {yab/} = father (HH), as in: {yab yum/} = parents (also refers to a deity with consort); {kyi/} = {'brel sgra/}; {mtshan/} = name (H) as in: {rgyu mtshan/} = reason, {mtshan nyid/} = characteristic, definition\n-----\nExample: [sound:3-4b.mp3]\n {mi 'gyur rin po che'i yab kyi mtshan ga re red zer na sprul sku o rgyan rin po che red/}  What is the name of {mi 'gyur rin po che/}’s father? (HH) It’s {sprul sku o rgyan rin po che/}.
mother’s name|[sound:3-5a.mp3]\n{yum gyi mtshan/} Mother’s name (HH)\nSyllables: {yum/} = mother (HH), as in: {yum chen mo/} = Prajñaparamita, the Great Mother; {gyi/} = {'brel sgra/} particle; {mtshan/} = name (H) as in: {rgyu mtshan/} = reason, {mtshan nyid/} = characteristic, definition\n-----\nExample: [sound:3-5b.mp3]\n {nga'i bsam tshul la sangs rgyas kyi yum gyi mtshan de snying rje po gcig 'dug_sgyu ma lha mdzes red/}  In my opinion, the name of the Buddha’s mother is beautiful - it’s Maya Devi. (HH)
birthplace|[sound:3-6a.mp3]\n{'khrungs sa/} Birthplace, place of birth (H)\nSyllables: {'khrungs pa/} = to be born (H), as in: {'khrungs skar dus chen/} = festival of the birthday (of some important person); {sa/} = place, earth, as in: {sa chu me rlung nam mkha'/} = earth, water, fire, wind and space; {lha sa/} = the place of the god(s)\n-----\nExample: [sound:3-6b.mp3]\n {khyed rang sangs rgyas kyi 'khrungs sa mjal myong yod pas/_lags yod/_na ning gnas de mjal pa yin/}  Have you ever visited the Buddha’s birthplace? - Yes, I visited this sacred place last year. (H)
place of birth|[sound:3-6a.mp3]\n{'khrungs sa/} Birthplace, place of birth (H)\nSyllables: {'khrungs pa/} = to be born (H), as in: {'khrungs skar dus chen/} = festival of the birthday (of some important person); {sa/} = place, earth, as in: {sa chu me rlung nam mkha'/} = earth, water, fire, wind and space; {lha sa/} = the place of the god(s)\n-----\nExample: [sound:3-6b.mp3]\n {khyed rang sangs rgyas kyi 'khrungs sa mjal myong yod pas/_lags yod/_na ning gnas de mjal pa yin/}  Have you ever visited the Buddha’s birthplace? - Yes, I visited this sacred place last year. (H)
place|[sound:3-7a.mp3]\n{sa phyogs/} Place, area\nSyllables: {sa/} = place, earth, as in: ({sa/} = place, earth, as in {sa bcu/} = the ten bodhisattva grounds, {sa snum/} = petroleum; {phyogs/} = direction, as in: {nub phyogs/} = the west, western direction, {phyogs ris/} = partiality\n-----\nExample: [sound:3-7b.mp3]\n {bkra shis lhun po dgon pa de/_bod kyi sa phyogs ga par la yod red/_ngas byas na dbus gtsang phyogs la yod red bsam gyi 'dug}  In which area of Tibet is Tashi Lhunpo monastery? If you ask me, I think it’s in the Central Tibetan area.
area|[sound:3-7a.mp3]\n{sa phyogs/} Place, area\nSyllables: {sa/} = place, earth, as in: ({sa/} = place, earth, as in {sa bcu/} = the ten bodhisattva grounds, {sa snum/} = petroleum; {phyogs/} = direction, as in: {nub phyogs/} = the west, western direction, {phyogs ris/} = partiality\n-----\nExample: [sound:3-7b.mp3]\n {bkra shis lhun po dgon pa de/_bod kyi sa phyogs ga par la yod red/_ngas byas na dbus gtsang phyogs la yod red bsam gyi 'dug}  In which area of Tibet is Tashi Lhunpo monastery? If you ask me, I think it’s in the Central Tibetan area.
southern nepal|[sound:3-8a.mp3]\n{bal yul gyi lho phyogs/} Southern Nepal\nSyllables: {bal yul/} = Nepal; {bal/} = wool; {yul/} = land, area; {gyi/} = {'brel sgra/}; {lho/} = south, as in: {lho 'dzam bu gling /} = the world; {phyogs/} = direction, as in {shar phyogs/} = east, eastern direction, {tshur phyogs/} = this side\n-----\nExample: [sound:3-8b.mp3]\n {sangs rgyas kyi sku bltam sa de deng sang bal yul gyi lho phyogs la yod red/_yin na'i sangs rgyas phar 'khrungs dus bal yul zer ba'i rgyal khab yod ma red/}  The Buddha’s birthplace is now in the south of Nepal. (HH) But when the Buddha was born there, there was no country called “Nepal”. (H)
indian border|[sound:3-9a.mp3]\n{rgya gar gyi sa mtshams/} Indian border\nSyllables: {rgya gar/} = India; {rgya/} = vast; {gar/} comes from: {dkar po/} = white; {gyi/}= {'brel sgra/} particle; {sa/} = place; {mtshams/} = border, as in: {mtshams la sdod pa/} = to stay in retreat\n-----\nExample: [sound:3-9b.mp3]\n {lum+bi ni nas rgya gar gyi sa mtshams bar du thag ring lod yod red/_thag ring po khyon nas yod ma red/_thag nye po yod red/}  How far is Lumbini from the Indian border? - Not far at all, it’s close.
the level of buddhahood|[sound:3-10a.mp3]\n{sangs rgyas kyi go 'phang /} The level of Buddhahood, the state of Buddhahood\nSyllables: {sangs rgyas/} = Buddha, {sangs/} = having purified, {rgyas/} = having developed, as in: {yar rgyas 'gro ba/} = to get better, to improve; {kyi/} = {'brel sgra/}; {go 'phang /} = level, state; {go/} = to hear, understand; {'phang /} = height\n-----\nExample: [sound:3-10b.mp3]\n {nga'i bsam tshul la sangs rgyas kyi go 'phang 'thob 'dod yod na nyams len mang po zhe po gcig byed dgos kyi yod sa red}  In my opinion, if one wants to obtain the level of Buddhahood, one probably has to practice a whole lot.
the state of buddhahood|[sound:3-10a.mp3]\n{sangs rgyas kyi go 'phang /} The level of Buddhahood, the state of Buddhahood\nSyllables: {sangs rgyas/} = Buddha, {sangs/} = having purified, {rgyas/} = having developed, as in: {yar rgyas 'gro ba/} = to get better, to improve; {kyi/} = {'brel sgra/}; {go 'phang /} = level, state; {go/} = to hear, understand; {'phang /} = height\n-----\nExample: [sound:3-10b.mp3]\n {nga'i bsam tshul la sangs rgyas kyi go 'phang 'thob 'dod yod na nyams len mang po zhe po gcig byed dgos kyi yod sa red}  In my opinion, if one wants to obtain the level of Buddhahood, one probably has to practice a whole lot.
age|[sound:3-11a.mp3]\n{dgung lo/} Age, year (H)\nSyllables: {dgung lo/} (H) = {lo/} = year, as in: {lo gsar/} = New Year\n-----\nExample: [sound:3-11b.mp3]\n {bstan 'dzin lags kyi rmo lags dgung lo chen po yin tsang /_mos khong la zhabs 'degs yag po zhu gi yod red/}  Since Tenzin-la’s grandmother is elderly, takes good care of her. (H) (h)
