king's palace|[sound:3-12a.mp3]\n{rgyal po'i khab/} King's palace, king's residence\nSyllables: {rgyal po/} = king, as in: {chos rgyal gsum/} = the Three Dharma Kings (or Skt. dharmarājas), {rgyal sa/} = capital, {nga rgyal/} = pride; {'i/} = {'brel sgra}; {khab/} = residence, palace, as in: {rgyal khab/} = nation, also: needle, as in: {khab rgyag pa/} = to give an injection\n-----\nExample: [sound:3-12b.mp3]\n {rgyal po'i khab la mthun rkyen yag po zhe drags yod na yang sangs rgyas phar bzhugs dus thugs mnyes po gnang yod ma red/}  Even though the facilities at the king’s residence were excellent, the Buddha was not happy living there. (H)
