the five common|[sound:3-13a.mp3]\n{thun mong gi rig gnas lnga/} The five common, ordinary, general, traditional sciences\nSyllables: {thun mong /} = common, ordinary; {gi/} = {'brel sgra/}; {rig gnas/} = science; {rig} = knowledge, intelligence, as in: {rig pa spyang po/} = clever, intelligent; {gnas/} = to abide, as in: {gnas stangs/} = situation, {zhi gnas/} = calm abiding; {lnga/} = five, as in: {tshes pa bco lnga/} = the 15th day of the Tibetan lunar month\n-----\nExample: [sound:3-13b.mp3]\n {sangs rgyas dgung lo gzhon gzhon yin dus/_thun mong gi rig gnas lnga yi slob sbyong gnang ya'i go skabs rag pa red/}  When the Buddha was young, he had the chance to study the five common sciences. (H)
