constituting cause|[sound:3-251a.mp3]\n{rgyu/} Cause, causality, root, primary/constituting cause\nSyllables: as in: {las rgyu 'bras/} = karma, cause and effect; {rgyu mtshan/} = reason\n-----\nExample: [sound:3-251b.mp3]\n {nang chos la rgyu dang rkyen gyi skor la mang po bris gnang yod pa de nga la dpe yag po mthong gi 'dug_gang yin zer na so so'i sdug bsngal gyi rgyu de ngos 'dzin byas na ma gtogs spang yag khag po 'dug ga}  It seems great to me that in Buddhism there is a lot written about causes and conditions. (H) Because it is hard to get rid of suffering unless one identifies its roots, right?
