what is to be realized|[sound:3-253a.mp3]\n{rtogs bya/} What is to be realized, what is to be thoroughly understood\nSyllables: {rtogs pa/} = to realize, as in: {spang rtogs kyi yon tan/} = the qualities of renunciation and realization; {bya/} = that which needs to be [done], as in: {bya ba/} = action, activity, {bya tshig} = verb, {shes bya/} = what is to be known\n-----\nExample: [sound:3-253b.mp3]\n {rtogs bya ze lab dus bya zer yag de bya ba dang gcig pa red pas/_gcig pa gcig rkyang ma red/_skabs 'dir ga re rtogs yag yod pa dang rtogs dgos kyi yod pa la go gi yod red/}  When we say {rtogs bya/} (that which is to be realized), the {bya/} is the same as in {bya ba/} (activity)? - It’s not exactly the same. In this context it refers to what is to be realized, what needs to be realized.
