to recognize|[sound:3-327a.mp3]\n{ngos 'dzin byed pa/} To recognize, to identify, to consider, to point out, to acknowledge\nSyllables: {ngos/} = side, surface; {'dzin pa/} = to hold, grasp, as in: {'dzin grwa/} = class, {bstan 'dzin/} = holder of the teaching, {blo la 'dzin pa/} = to memorize, keep in mind; {byed pa/} = verbalizer, to do, as in: {yid ches byed pa/} = to trust\n-----\nExample: [sound:3-327b.mp3]\n {skye rga na 'chi'i sdug bsngal cha tshang ba spong 'dod yod na dang po ni de tsho'i rgyu dang 'byung sa ngos 'dzin byed dgos kyi yod sa red bsam gyi 'dug}  If one wishes to give up all the suffering of birth, old age, sickness and death, one probably needs to identify their causes and origins first, I believe.
