ornament of realisation|[sound:3-357a.mp3]\n{sher phyin mngon rtogs rgyan/} Ornament of Realisation, Abhisamayālaṃkāra, a commentary on the Prajñāpāramitā, Perfection of Wisdom\nSyllables: {sher phyin/} = prajñāpāramitā; {sher/} = {shes rab/} = insight; {phyin/} = went, as in: {pha rol tu phyin pa/} = pāramitā; {mngon/} = manifest, as in: {mngon sum/} = direct, as in: {mngon sum dang rjes dpag tshad ma/} = direct and inferential valid cognition; {rtogs pa/} = to realise, as in: {spang rtogs kyi yon tan/} = the qualities of renunciation and realisation; {rgyan/} = ornament, as in: {rna rgyan/} = earring, {rgyan tshig} = adjective\n-----\nExample: [sound:3-357b.mp3]\n {byams pa mgon pos brtsams gnang ba'i chos chen po lnga yi nang nas gcig sher phyin mngon rtogs rgyan red/}  Among the Five Great Dharmas which the Protector Maitreya has composed, one is the Ornament of Realisation. (H)
