insight|[sound:3-359a.mp3]\n{shes rab/} insight, knowledge, discriminative wisdom or awareness, prajña, understanding\nSyllables: {shes pa/} = to know, as in {ye shes/} = primordial wisdom; {rab/} = completely, as in: {ya rab spyod bzang /} = excellent conduct, {rab tu 'byung ba/} = to become a monastic\n-----\nExample: [sound:3-359b.mp3]\n {thos bsam sgom gsum gyi skor la sbyang dus rgan lags kyis ga re gsungs song zer na thos pa las byung ba'i shes rab dang /_bsam pa las byung ba'i shes rab dang /_sgom pa las byung ba'i shes rab gsum yod red ze 'grel bshad bskyon song /}  When I was learning about the three, study, reflection and meditation, what did our dear teacher say? (H) She explained that there is insight which comes from study, insight which results from contemplation and insight gained from meditation. (H)
