the mind which unites|[sound:3-361a.mp3]\n{zung du 'jug pa/} the mind which unites, which unifies, which is a unity [of the two – compassion and insight]\nSyllables: {zung 'jug} = union, unity, as in: {gsal stong zung 'jug} = unity of clarity and emptiness; {zung /} = pair, two; {du/} = {la don/}; {'jug pa/} = to enter, to engage, as in: {sngon 'jug} = prefix, {rjes 'jug} = suffix, {rtags kyi 'jug pa/} = Application of Genders\n-----\nExample: [sound:3-361b.mp3]\n {nang chos kyi nang la zung du 'jug pa kha shas kyi skor gsung gi yod red/_dper na shes rab dang snying rje zung du 'jug pa dang /_gsal stong zung du 'jug pa la sogs pa/}  In Buddhism they talk about various “unities”, for example, the unity of wisdom and compassion and the union of clarity and emptiness.
