commentary|[sound:3-364a.mp3]\n{bstan bcos/} commentary, treatise, śāstra, philosophical treatise\nSyllables: {bstan/} = taught, as in: {bstan 'dzin/} = holder of the teaching; {bcos/} = fabricated, as in: {sman bcos byed pa/} = to cure, treat a disease\n-----\nExample: [sound:3-364b.mp3]\n {nga'i bsam tshul la rgya gar dang bod kyi slob dpon dang mkhas dbang gis brtsams pa'i bstan bcos de tsho ga tshod snyan po yod na yang sangs rgyas kyis gsungs pa'i mdo nang bzhin byin rlabs chen po yod kyi ma red/}  In my opinion, the commentaries composed by the great Indian and Tibetan masters and learned ones, no matter how interesting they are, might not have the same blessings as the sūtras spoken by the Buddha. (H)
treatise|[sound:3-364a.mp3]\n{bstan bcos/} commentary, treatise, śāstra, philosophical treatise\nSyllables: {bstan/} = taught, as in: {bstan 'dzin/} = holder of the teaching; {bcos/} = fabricated, as in: {sman bcos byed pa/} = to cure, treat a disease\n-----\nExample: [sound:3-364b.mp3]\n {nga'i bsam tshul la rgya gar dang bod kyi slob dpon dang mkhas dbang gis brtsams pa'i bstan bcos de tsho ga tshod snyan po yod na yang sangs rgyas kyis gsungs pa'i mdo nang bzhin byin rlabs chen po yod kyi ma red/}  In my opinion, the commentaries composed by the great Indian and Tibetan masters and learned ones, no matter how interesting they are, might not have the same blessings as the sūtras spoken by the Buddha. (H)
