king-like bodhicitta|[sound:3-365a.mp3]\n{rgyal po lta bu'i sems bskyed/} king-like bodhicitta\nSyllables: {rgyal po/} = king, as in: {phyi rgyal/} = abroad, {rgyal sa/} = capital, {chos rgyal gsum/} = the three Dharma kings; {lta bu/} = like, as in: {khong khro lta bu'i sdig pa med//} = “there is no evil like anger”; {'i/} = {'brel sgra/}; {sems bskyed/} = bodhicitta\n-----\nExample: [sound:3-365b.mp3]\n {rgyal po lta bu'i sems bskyed ni dang po so so sangs rgyas kyi go 'phang thob byas/_de'i rjes la gzhi nas sems can thams cad sa de la 'god 'dod pa'i bsam pa/}  King-like bodhicitta is the thought that wishes to first attain the state of Buddhahood oneself and only after that establish all sentient beings in that state.
ferryman-like bodhicitta|[sound:3-366a.mp3]\n{mnyan pa lta bu'i sems bskyed/} ferryman-like bodhicitta\nSyllables: {mnyan pa/} = ferryman, {mnyan/} = boat, {pa/} = {bdag sgra/}, makes it into the owner/person; {lta bu'i sems bskyed/} = -like bodhicitta, see above\n-----\nExample: [sound:3-366b.mp3]\n {mnyan pa lta bu'i sems bskyed gang 'dras gcig red zer na rang dang sems can thams cad dus gcig la sangs rgyas kyi sa la slebs par byed 'dod pa'i bsam pa/}  If one were to ask what ferryman-like bodhicitta is, it is the thought that wishes oneself and all other sentient beings reach the state of Buddhahood at the same time.
shepherd-like bodhicitta|[sound:3-367a.mp3]\n{rdzi bo lta bu'i sems bskyed/} shepherd-like bodhicitta\nSyllables: {rdzi bo/} = shepherd; {lta bu'i sems bskyed/} = -like bodhicitta\n-----\nExample: [sound:3-367b.mp3]\n {rdzi bo lta bu'i sems bskyed ni rang gi sngon la sems can thams cad sangs rgyas kyi go 'phang la 'god 'dod pa'i bsam pa de red/}  Shepherd-like bodhicitta is the thought of wishing to establish all sentient beings in a state of Buddhahood before oneself.
the state of buddhahood|[sound:3-368a.mp3]\n{sangs rgyas kyi go 'phang /} the state of Buddhahood, full enlightenment, level of Buddhahood\nSyllables: {sangs rgyas/} = Buddha; {kyi/} = {'brel sgra}; {go/} = occasion, as in: {go skabs/} = opportunity; {'phang /} = height\n-----\nExample: [sound:3-368b.mp3]\n {mdo yi lam gyi dbang du byas na bskal pa grangs med par bsod nams dang ye shes kyi tshogs bsags pa'i rjes la gzhi nas sangs rgyas kyi go 'phang 'thob yag yod red/}  From a sūtra path perspective, the state of Buddhahood is only to be reached after having gathered the accumulations of merit and wisdom during countless eons.
full enlightenment|[sound:3-368a.mp3]\n{sangs rgyas kyi go 'phang /} the state of Buddhahood, full enlightenment, level of Buddhahood\nSyllables: {sangs rgyas/} = Buddha; {kyi/} = {'brel sgra}; {go/} = occasion, as in: {go skabs/} = opportunity; {'phang /} = height\n-----\nExample: [sound:3-368b.mp3]\n {mdo yi lam gyi dbang du byas na bskal pa grangs med par bsod nams dang ye shes kyi tshogs bsags pa'i rjes la gzhi nas sangs rgyas kyi go 'phang 'thob yag yod red/}  From a sūtra path perspective, the state of Buddhahood is only to be reached after having gathered the accumulations of merit and wisdom during countless eons.
