intent|[sound:3-369a.mp3]\n{'god 'dod pa'i kun slong /} intent, motivation which aspires, wishes to establish\nSyllables: {'god pa/} = to arrange, establish, as in: {'jig rten 'god pa po/} = creator of the world; {'dod pa/} = to wish, as in: {snying 'dod pa/} = to really want; {'i/} = {'brel sgra/}; {kun slong /} = motivation, intent, see above\n-----\nExample: [sound:3-369b.mp3]\n {ngas byas na rang gi sngon la sems can gzhan dag de tsho sangs rgyas kyi sa la 'god 'dod pa'i kun slong de lug rdzi lta bu'i sems bskyed ni hang sang yag gcig red pa/}  If you ask me, the motivation which aspires to establish all other sentient beings in a state of Buddhahood before oneself, shepherd-like bodhicitta, is incredible, isn’t it?
