to practice|[sound:3-370a.mp3]\n{chos sgrub pa/} to practice, accomplish the Dharma\nSyllables: {chos/} = Dharma, as in: {chos lugs/} = religious tradition; {sgrub pa/} = to accomplish, as in {tshig sgrub/} = sentence\n-----\nExample: [sound:3-370b.mp3]\n {nga'i chos grogs kha shas kyi bsam tshul la chos sgrub 'dod yod na nges par du dben gyi sa cha la phyin byas/_brag phug gi nang la lo mang po'i ring la mtshams la bsdad dgos kyi yod red/}  According to the opinion of some of my Dharma friends, if one wants to practice Dharma, one really needs to go to a solitary place and stay in a retreat in a cave for many years.
