somebody who lacks experience|[sound:3-407a.mp3]\n{nyams myong med mkhan/} somebody who lacks experience, an inexperienced person, a person who does not have experience\nSyllables: {nyams myong /} = experience; {nyams pa/} = to degenerate, as in: {nyams gso byed pa/} = to renovate; {myong ba/} = to experience, to have ever done; {med mkhan/} = somebody who does not have, {med/} = not, as in: {sha med/} = vegetarian; {mkhan/} = nominaliser, as in: {mkhan po/} = monastic teacher\n-----\nExample: [sound:3-407b.mp3]\n {nyams myong med mkhan yin na dang po sgom rgyag dus rnam rtog de tsho mang ru 'gro gi yod pa'i tshor snang slebs kyi red/_yin na'i de bden pa ma red/_yin na'i thengs ma dang po rnam rtog mang po yod pa de mthong gi yod red/}  For somebody who lacks experience, when first meditating, it feels as if one’s discursive thoughts are [even] increasing. However, that is not true, but it’s the first time that one sees that there are many thoughts.
