immeasurable love|[sound:3-459a.mp3]\n{byams pa tshad med/} Immeasurable Love, Immeasurable Loving Kindness, Immeasurable Maitrī\nSyllables: {byams pa/} = loving kindness, as in: {byams brtse/} = love and affection, {byams pa mgon po/} = the Protector Maitreya; {tshad med/} = immeasurable\n-----\nExample: [sound:3-459b.mp3]\n {spyir btang gi byams brtse dang byams pa tshad med gnyis kyi bar ru la khyad par ga re yod red/_byams pa tshad med zer yag de la tshad yod ma red/_sems can thams cad la a ma lags gcig gi so so'i spu gu la yod pa'i byams pa dang gcig pa red/}  Generally speaking, what is the difference between the two, love and affection and Immeasurable Love? There is no limit to what we call “Immeasurable Love”. It is the same love as a mother has for her [only] child - for all sentient beings.
