peace and happiness of mind; mental peace and wellbeing|[sound:3-477a.mp3]\n{sems kyi zhi bde/} peace and happiness of mind; mental peace and wellbeing\nSyllables: {sems/} = heart, mind; {kyi/} = {'brel sgra/}; {zhi bde/} = peace and happiness, {zhi/} = peace, as in: {zhi gnas/} = calm abiding, {rgyal sras zhi ba lha/} = The Son of the Victorious Ones, Śāntideva; {bde/} = well, comfortable, as in: {blo bde po/} = relaxed, {go bde po/} = lucid, {stabs bde po/} = convenient\n-----\nExample: [sound:3-477b.mp3]\n {\u0f38rgyal ba rin po ches brtsams gnang ba'i phyag deb mang po'i nang nas nga'i dga' shos ni sems kyi zhi bde de red/}  Among the many books which His Holiness the XIV Dalai Lama has composed, my favorite is Peace and Happiness of Mind. (H)
a society which is characterized by peace and wellbeing; a peaceful and happy society|[sound:3-478a.mp3]\n{zhi bde ldan pa'i spyi tshogs/} a society which is characterized by peace and wellbeing; a peaceful and happy society\nSyllables: {zhi bde/} = peace and happiness; {ldan pa/} = endowed with, as in: {dga' ldan/} = Tuṣita, {bcom ldan 'das/} = The Transcendent Conqueror; {'i/} = {'brel sgra/}; {spyi tshogs/} = society, {spyi/} = in general, as in: {spyir btang /} = generally, {spyi zla/} = international month, {tshogs/} = collection, as in: {tshogs 'du/} = meeting, {bsod nams kyi tshogs/} = the accumulation of merit and {ye shes kyi tshogs/} = the accumulation of wisdom\n-----\nExample: [sound:3-478b.mp3]\n {nga'i bsam tshul la chos lugs tshang ma'i dmigs yul gcig pa red/_gnas skabs su so so rang la bde ba thob pa dang /_mthar thug ni zhi bde dang ldan pa'i spyi tshogs dang 'dzam gling gcig skrun yag de red/}  In my opinion, the aim of all religious traditions is the same: one obtains one’s own temporary happiness and, ultimately, brings about a society and world of peace and wellbeing.
remedy|[sound:3-479a.mp3]\n{gnyen po/} remedy, antidote, counteragent, antithesis\nSyllables: As in: {gnyen po bsten pa/} = to apply, rely on the antidote\n-----\nExample: [sound:3-479b.mp3]\n {nyon mongs gcig skye 'gro'o yin dus ngos 'dzin byed thub na a ni lam sang gnyen po bsten na des rang gzhan gnyis ka la gnod pa chen po skyel thub kyi ma red bsam gyi 'dug}  If one is able to immediately identify and apply the antidote as soon as an affliction has arisen, then it won’t be able to cause a lot of harm to oneself and others, I believe.
