to bring unease|[sound:3-488a.mp3]\n{ma zhi bar byed pa/} to bring unease, disturb, shatter the peace, make uneasy, uncomfortable\nSyllables: {ma/} = {dgag sgra/}, as in: {gangs ma char/} = neither snow nor rain, meaning both together; {zhi ba/} = peace, as in: {'dzam gling gi zhi bde'i ded dpon/} = advocate of peace in [this] world; {ra/} = {la don/}; {byed pa/} = verbalizer, as in: {thag chod byed pa/} = to decide\n-----\nExample: [sound:3-488b.mp3]\n {nga tsho'i sems ma zhi bar byed mkhan gtso bo ngos 'dzin byed 'dod yod na sgom brgyab na ma gtogs ha go yag khag po yod sa red bsam gyi 'dug}  I think that if one wants to identify what the main thing is which makes the mind unpeaceful, unless one meditates, it is difficult to find out.
