without any notion of attachment or aversion|[sound:3-489a.mp3]\n{chags sdang med par/} without any notion of attachment or aversion, free from desire and hatred\nSyllables: {chags/} = short form of {'dod chags/} = attachment, desire, as in: {chags pa/} = to be attached; {med pa/} = without, as in: {re dogs med pa/} without hopes and fears; {ra/} = {la don/}\n-----\nExample: [sound:3-489b.mp3]\n {mi tshang mas so so'i grogs po grogs mo dang dgra po la chags sdang med pa thog nas btang snyoms gcig sems nang la bskyed thub pa yin na 'dzam gling la zhi bde yong srid pa red/}  If everyone was able to cultivate inclusiveness in their heart, free from aversion towards enemies and attachments towards friends, then peace and wellbeing would be possible in the world.
